  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Leland Fellowship</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Uganda, the Fellow will be integrated into the Resilient livelihoods program team where they will work on two existing initiatives &#x2013; Urban Food Hives and the SEEDS program.

&#x2022; The Urban Food Hives work is centered on the creation of stronger food systems in major urban centers in Uganda. The Uganda team aims for Effective and Inclusive Food Governance in Kampala and Soroti to sustainably deliver safe and nutritious foods for all amidst climate change challenges and pandemic. As part of the UFH team in Uganda, the Fellow will help plan, coordinate and implement pilot activities, including:
o Organize, preside on discussions and attend dialogues withpartners including the government.
o Manage UFH&apos;s grant writing and reporting processes, including supporting the development of grant proposals and as needed with research and writing.
o Contribute to knowledge generation, knowledge exchange and knowledge transfer activities across UFH pilot countries.
o Develop and write stories on the lessons from the UFH pilots bringing out the various models (to show proof of concept).
o Support partnership engagements and ensuring that the UFH is represented in a way that aligns with UFH framework and Oxfam values.

&#x2022; The &#x201c;Partnership for Diversity Program&#x201d; aims at developing new partnership models for agricultural research (&#x201c;Partnership for Diversity Program&#x201d;). The goal is to pilot social and institutional innovations and participatory research approached to shift the current power dynamics and strengthen the role of farmers in seed systems.

By Sept 2023, both initiatives will be well-grounded, and the Fellow will provide overall support that could include development of communications materials, monitoring and evaluation, partnership outreach, coordination across partners, drafting of advocacy materials and grant management functions.</narrative>
  </description>
